4.7
Implement Penetration testing

-------------------------------

Lesson Summary
The underlying OS/platform directly affects host vulnerabilities. How the OS is configured is crucial.
Software vulnerability known as "zero-day" has an effect that is long-lasting. This happens before the vulnerability is publicly known. Other vulnerabilities are "improper input handling", "improper error handling", "resource exhaustion", "race condition", and "memory vulnerabilities''.
Some encryption solutions are insecure or become insecure over time. The poor implementation also reveals weaknesses.
A security assessment is a process of testing security controls to expose any weaknesses or gaps in your tools, technologies, services, and operations.
Vulnerability assessment tools are vulnerability scanner, port scanner, protocol/packet analyzer, fingerprinting tools, network enumerator, password cracker, backup utilities and honeypot.
Penetration testing verifies that a threat exists, and exploits any vulnerabilities. One of the tools are stress testers, and with this, you test your systems' ability to respond to increased computing overhead and network bandwidth.

